    "description": "Fort McKavett SHS is a historic cultural resource site operated by the Texas Historical Commission. It tells the story of the western Texas Hill Country Frontier with a specific focus on mid- to late-19th Century defensive military operations from 1852 to 1883. The site is the best preserved Indian Wars-era fort in Texas with over 19 original structures, including several officers quarters, an original Post Headquarters and Enlisted Barracks, an 1870's hospital and schoolhouse, a limestone quarry and kiln, and several ruins. The remote 90+ acres site offers picturesque Texas Hill Country vistas, incredible dark sky experiences, and a quiet & peaceful environment.",
